---
title: Patty Melt
servings: 1
course: lunch
cuisine: American
tags: quick, one-pan, fried, beef, bread
image: https://img.youtube.com/vi/M-PuGg7Ek-w/maxresdefault.jpg
source: https://youtu.be/M-PuGg7Ek-w
time: 15m
---

Preheat a #frying pan{} over medium-high heat. Melt half of the @butter{15%g} in the pan and toast the @white bread{2%slices} on both sides until golden. Remove the bread and set aside.

Slice the @brown onion{0.5}. Add the @vegetable oil{1%tbsp} and the remaining @butter{10%g} to the pan. Add the sliced onion along with a pinch of @salt{0.5%tsp}. Cook over medium-high heat, stirring constantly, until nicely caramelized. Transfer the onions directly onto one slice of the toasted bread, leaving any rendered fat in the pan.

In a #bowl{}, combine the @mayonnaise{2%tbsp}, @chipotle in adobo{1%tsp}, @garlic powder{0.25%tsp}, @mustard powder{0.25%tsp}, @black pepper{0.25%tsp}, @white pepper{0.25%tsp}, @msg{1%pinch}, and @white distilled vinegar{1%tsp}. Mix well, then spread the sauce onto the second slice of toasted bread.

Divide the @beef mince{200%g} into two balls. Return the frying pan to high heat and sprinkle with a pinch of @&salt{0.25%tsp}. Place the beef balls into the pan and season the tops with another pinch of @&salt{0.25%tsp}. Let sit for ~{30%seconds}, then firmly smash each ball flat with a #spatula{} so they match the shape of the bread.

Cook until a deep crust forms, then flip both patties. Place a @cheese{2} onto each patty and let melt.

Transfer the patties onto the caramelized onions. Top with the sauced slice of bread, cut in half, and serve.
